{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"reviews\":[{\"id\":\"structural_monotony\",\"verdict\":\"insufficient_evidence\",\"rationale\":\"The clearance may be right, but a whole-document shape judgment needed explicit comparison across major sections and the annotator supplied none.\",\"evidence\":[\"The goals are to:\",\"A) Identity program\",\"2) A public mailing list so you can interact among yourselves. \",\"B) Designated observer at W3C Advisory Committee Meetings\"]},{\"id\":\"tonal_uniformity\",\"verdict\":\"undercall\",\"rationale\":\"The document largely stays in one formal institutional register; the annotator's claim that the register breaks at least once is not borne out by the text as a whole.\",\"evidence\":[\"Dear W3C Invited Expert,\",\"Further to input from the W3C Advisory Board, we are rolling out a W3C Invited Expert identity program.\",\"We have several months until the 7-9 April 2019 Advisory Committee Meeting in Quebec, Canada, to make adjustments and announce the program and particularly the IE observer to the W3C Advisory Committee. \",\"Thank you!\"]},{\"id\":\"faux_specificity\",\"verdict\":\"insufficient_evidence\",\"rationale\":\"The no-finding judgment is plausible because the email is procedural rather than scene-based, but the annotator gave no textual support for clearing the item.\",\"evidence\":[\"A public directory of W3C Invited Experts\",\"A public mailing list so you can interact among yourselves.\",\"Designated observer at W3C Advisory Committee Meetings\"]},{\"id\":\"neutrality_collapse\",\"verdict\":\"insufficient_evidence\",\"rationale\":\"The text does appear to advance a concrete program rather than flattening into both-sides framing, but the annotator did not document that stance with evidence.\",\"evidence\":[\"we are rolling out a W3C Invited Expert identity program.\",\"we have created:\",\"W3C Invited Experts may designate one individual amongst themselves\"]},{\"id\":\"even_jargon_distribution\",\"verdict\":\"misclassified\",\"rationale\":\"The text is clear of the flagged defect, but the chosen category is wrong: jargon is not clumped in one expert-heavy pocket, it is distributed throughout the email in a genre-natural way.\",\"evidence\":[\"W3C Invited Expert identity program\",\"A public directory of W3C Invited Experts\",\"Designated observer at W3C Advisory Committee Meetings\",\"w3c-ac-forum [2], the list for discussion among W3C Advisory Committee Members and the Advisory Board on matters of relevance to W3C.\"]},{\"id\":\"forced_synesthesia\",\"verdict\":\"insufficient_evidence\",\"rationale\":\"There is probably no forced cross-modal imagery here, but the annotator provided no support for clearing the judgment.\",\"evidence\":[\"The goals are to:\",\"A public directory of W3C Invited Experts\",\"That non-voting individual represents the interests of W3C Invited Experts\"]},{\"id\":\"generic_metaphors\",\"verdict\":\"undercall\",\"rationale\":\"The document contains at least one generic institutional metaphor that could have been flagged.\",\"evidence\":[\"we are rolling out a W3C Invited Expert identity program.\"]},{\"id\":\"referential_clarity\",\"verdict\":\"insufficient_evidence\",\"rationale\":\"The clearance may be defensible, but the annotator did not show that potentially vague references and definite descriptions were checked across the document.\",\"evidence\":[\"That page exposes a combination of W3C database information and information you may enter via your W3C profile:\",\"When a participant is granted IE status, our system sends a notification e-mail. We’ll update that text to inform IEs of this program and will point to the new “about” page.\",\"To that effect, a straw-man proposal is for the designated Invited Expert self-declares to <\"]},{\"id\":\"formulaic_parallelism\",\"verdict\":\"insufficient_evidence\",\"rationale\":\"A no-finding answer is plausible, but the annotator supplied no textual basis for clearing repeated syntactic or slogan-like symmetry.\",\"evidence\":[\"The goals are to:\",\"A) Give IEs a sense of group identity.\",\"B) Give a slot at all AC meetings for the Invited Experts to send someone as an observer.\"]},{\"id\":\"semantic_redundancy\",\"verdict\":\"insufficient_evidence\",\"rationale\":\"The document may avoid meaningful redundancy, but the annotator gave no evidence showing that repeated summaries or restatements were checked.\",\"evidence\":[\"A) Identity program\",\"2) A public mailing list so you can interact among yourselves. \",\"Over the next few weeks, I invite you to get back to me about improvements to the web pages (content, layout) and more generally to the identity program itself\"]},{\"id\":\"underspecified_language\",\"verdict\":\"supported\",\"rationale\":\"The annotator correctly identifies a vague evaluative phrase whose success condition is never defined.\",\"evidence\":[\"successfully rely on local mail filters\"]},{\"id\":\"context_leakage\",\"verdict\":\"overcall\",\"rationale\":\"The flagged sentence does not require missing chat context; within the email itself it simply discloses a drawback of the mailing-list setup and offers a practical workaround.\",\"evidence\":[\"2) A public mailing list so you can interact among yourselves. \",\"Any IE addition/removal is reflected live in the subscribers list.\",\"There is no opt-out, unfortunately, but I hope you can successfully rely on local mail filters.\"]},{\"id\":\"performed_candour\",\"verdict\":\"insufficient_evidence\",\"rationale\":\"No obvious candour-booster appears, but the annotator offered no textual support for clearing the item.\",\"evidence\":[\"Please, take a moment to review and update your profile and check the result in the directory.\",\"Thank you!\"]},{\"id\":\"vacuous_connection\",\"verdict\":\"insufficient_evidence\",\"rationale\":\"The no-finding judgment may be right, but the annotator did not substantiate it by checking the document's connective logic.\",\"evidence\":[\"When a participant is granted IE status, our system sends a notification e-mail. We’ll update that text to inform IEs of this program and will point to the new “about” page.\",\"To that effect, a straw-man proposal is for the designated Invited Expert self-declares to <\",\"Over the next few weeks, I invite you to get back to me about improvements to the web pages (content, layout) and more generally to the identity program itself\"]},{\"id\":\"genre_specific\",\"verdict\":\"insufficient_evidence\",\"rationale\":\"`default` is likely the right genre label for this institutional email, but the annotator gave no evidence for the classification or for clearing genre-specific concerns.\",\"evidence\":[\"Dear W3C Invited Expert,\",\"Further to input from the W3C Advisory Board, we are rolling out a W3C Invited Expert identity program.\",\"Coralie Mercier, Head of W3C Marketing & Communications\"]}]}"}}
